From: jraphaelsst <joaoraphaelsst@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 17:39:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(seed/testing): MockSupabaseClient cross-schema
 propagation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`MockSupabaseClient.schema(name)` previously created a scoped instance
with a fresh `_tables` dict — writes via `parent.set_table_data` were
invisible through `parent.schema("X").table("Y")` chains. Blocks Pin 5
invalid-sig tests for any webhook whose secret resolver hits a foreign
schema (ERP `_resolve_assinatura_secret` reads
`db.schema("core").table("org_settings")`).

Fix (Option B + shared backing dict):

- `_qualify(name)` normalizes bare table names to `<schema>.<table>`;
  names already containing `.` pass through.
- `_tables` is keyed by schema-qualified names.
- `table(name)` qualifies the lookup via bound schema.
- `set_table_data(name, data)` qualifies the storage key — accepts
  both bare names and `"<schema>.<table>"`.
- `schema(name)` returns a scoped view that SHARES `_tables`, `_rpcs`,
  `auth`, and `storage` with the parent — `set_table_data` on either
  side is mutually visible.

Backward-compat preserved: bare-name set + bare-name read on any bound
schema continues to round-trip through the same qualified key. All 78
pre-existing mock tests pass under the new model; 10 new tests cover
the cross-schema seams (parent ↔ scoped symmetry, schema isolation,
the exact two-step ERP webhook resolver shape, public-qualifier
equivalence, repeated scoping round-trip).

ERP Pin 5 invalid-sig tests for `assinaturas/webhook` +
`meta_api/webhook` (filed by Engineer SSS during the webhook-compliance
audit) are now unblocked at the seed-lib level; product-side test
additions deferred to a focused follow-up because this worktree's venv
can't load the ERP app (missing `xhtml2pdf` dep; pip install denied
out-of-scope by auto-mode).

Project: projects/mock-supabase-cross-schema-fix/PROJECT.md
Seed-lib regression: 1159 passed (88 mock-related: 78 pre-existing + 10 new).
AST-driven via libcst.

