+# mock-supabase-cross-schema-fix — Project Document
+
+- **Created:** 2026-05-11
+- **Last updated:** 2026-05-11
+- **Status:** Phases 0-2 shipped → Phase 3 deferred (env blocker)
+- **Owner / stakeholders:** USER · Engineer MOCK-SCHEMA (executor) · Engineer SSS (filer)
+- **Related docs:** `archive/projects/2026-05-11/21-webhook-compliance-audit-2026-05-11/PROJECT.md` (filing source); `seed/lib/backend/noctusai_lib/testing/mocks.py`
+- **Project slug:** `mock-supabase-cross-schema-fix` (cross-product / seed-lib scope — `projects/<slug>/`)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Context & Purpose
+
+Engineer SSS surfaced a mock-side gap during the webhook-compliance audit
+(`archive/projects/2026-05-11/21-webhook-compliance-audit-2026-05-11`):
+`MockSupabaseClient.schema(name)` previously created a scoped instance
+with a **fresh** `_tables` dict, so data seeded on the parent via
+`set_table_data` was invisible through `parent.schema("X").table("Y")`
+chains. ERP's `_resolve_assinatura_secret` resolver runs exactly that
+shape (`db.schema("core").table("org_settings")`), and the audit's
+attempt to add Pin 5 invalid-sig tests for `assinaturas/webhook` had
+to be reverted as a result. The gap also blocks any future webhook
+receiver whose secret lives in a non-bound schema.
+
+**Win:** seed-lib mock now models PostgREST's cross-schema reach
+correctly. ERP's deferred Pin 5 tests can land (Phase 3 carrier);
+no product-side workaround needed.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Confirmed constraints
+
+Lifted from the engineer brief (no live user interrogation — this was
+filed by a parallel engineer with full context):
+
+- **Design choice:** Option B (schema-qualified storage keys) was the
+  default recommendation, with a refinement we adopted — **B + shared
+  `_tables` backing dict via `schema()`**. Reason: B alone leaves
+  `parent.set_table_data("core.foo", ...)` and
+  `scoped.set_table_data("foo", ...)` reachable through different
+  qualification paths; the shared dict makes the symmetry total.
+- **Verification scope:** seed-lib pytest must stay green; ERP webhook
+  router tests can't be exercised in this worktree's venv (missing
+  product dep `xhtml2pdf`).
+- **Constraints inherited:** AST-first (libcst), no monkey-patching of
+  our code, no `--no-verify`, branch-only push, stage explicit paths.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Goal & non-goals
+
+**Goal:** restore mock fidelity for cross-schema lookups while
+preserving every existing call shape.
+
+**Non-goals:** changing the production Supabase client; adding new
+storage primitives unrelated to schema scoping; refactoring the
+72-test legacy mock surface.
+
+---
+
+## 3a. Seed-first analysis
+
+This IS the seed-first fix. The recurrence pattern (`.schema("X").table("Y")`)
+appears in ERP `_resolve_assinatura_secret`, `core/billing` (per the
+audit catalog), and any future webhook resolver that needs a cross-
+schema secret store. Fixing the mock at the seed eliminates **all**
+per-product workarounds (the alternative being product-side `monkey
+patch.setattr` or `set_table_data("org_settings", ...)` on a separately-
+constructed mock — both anti-pattern shape). Per-product code count for
+the fix: **zero**.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Approach (Phase plan)
+
+- **Phase 0 — Read.** `seed/lib/backend/noctusai_lib/testing/mocks.py`
+  lines 972-1061; trace `_builder_for` / `table` / `schema` /
+  `set_table_data` / `set_sequential_responses`.
+- **Phase 1 — Fix.** AST-driven (`libcst`) patch:
+  - Inject `_qualify(name)` helper.
+  - Rewrite `table` to qualify keys.
+  - Rewrite `schema` to share `_tables` + `_rpcs` + `auth` + `storage`.
+  - Rewrite `set_table_data` to qualify the storage key.
+- **Phase 2 — Tests.** New file
+  `seed/lib/backend/tests/testing/test_mocks.py`; 10 tests covering
+  backward-compat (bare-name round-trip on default + bound schemas),
+  cross-schema set/lookup, parent ↔ scoped symmetry, isolation across
+  schemas, and the exact two-step ERP webhook resolver shape.
+- **Phase 3 — Unblock ERP webhook tests** — **deferred** (env gap;
+  see §11 + §7).
+
+---
+
+## 5. Touch surfaces
+
+- **Edited:** `seed/lib/backend/noctusai_lib/testing/mocks.py`
+  (4 methods rewritten + 1 added; libcst-driven).
+- **Created:** `seed/lib/backend/tests/testing/test_mocks.py` (10 tests).
+- **Created:** `projects/mock-supabase-cross-schema-fix/PROJECT.md`,
